{
  "title": "Lateral Epicondylitis (Tennis Elbow)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3082/lateral-epicondylitis-tennis-elbow",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 5 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Lateral Epicondylitis (also known as Tennis Elbow) is an overuse injury caused by eccentric overload at the origin of the common extensor tendon, leading to tendinosis and inflammation of the ECRB.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness over the lateral epicondyle made worse with resisted wrist extension.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is primarily nonoperative with NSAIDs, activity modification, and bracing. Rarely, operative management is indicated for patients with persistent symptoms who fail nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common cause for elbow symptoms in patients with elbow pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "affects 1-3% of adults annually",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "commonly in dominant arm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "affects up to 50% of all tennis players",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "risk factors",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "poor swing technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "heavy racket",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "incorrect grip size",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "high string tension",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "common in laborers who utilize heavy tools",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "workers engaged in repetitive gripping or lifting tasks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most common between ages of 45 and 64 years old",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "men and women equally affected",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tenodesis effect to optimize grip causes overuse of ECRB",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "precipitated by repetitive wrist extension and forearm pronation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "common in tennis players (backhand implicated)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "thought to begin as a microtear of the origin of **ECRB**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may also involve microtears of ECRL and ECU",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "a degenerative process as opposed to an inflammatory process",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathohistology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "microscopic evaluation of the tissue reveals",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**angiofibroblastic hyperplasia**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/normal_tendon_elbow.jpg",
                          "caption": "normal tendon slide"
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/angiofibro_histo.jpg",
                          "caption": "angiofibroblastic tendon"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**disorganized collagen**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lacks inflammatory cells",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**radial tunnel syndrome** is present in 5%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Common extensor origin",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/elbow_anatomy1.jpg",
              "caption": "Anatomy of common extensor tendons"
            },
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/tennis%20elbow.jpg",
              "caption": "Shows Insertion of ECRB"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "muscles that originate from lateral supracondylar ridge",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extensor carpi radialis longus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "muscles that originate on lateral epicondyle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extensor carpi radialis brevis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "origin is a 13x7mm diamond-shaped area superior to the center of the epicondyle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tendon lies just superficial to the joint capsule",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "extensor carpi ulnaris",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "extensor digitorum",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "extensor digiti minimi",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anconeus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "shares same attachment site as ECRB",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ligaments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lateral ulnar collateral ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/lucl.jpg",
                  "caption": "Elbow lateral ligaments"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nerves",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior interosseus nerve (PIN) enters the supinator just distal to the radial head",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "compression can lead to radial tunnel syndrome (may co-exist with lateral epicondylitis)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain with **resisted wrist extension**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain with gripping activities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "decreased grip strength",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "palpation & inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**point tenderness** at ECRB insertion into lateral epicondyle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "few mm distal to tip of lateral epicondyle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neuromuscular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may have **decreased grip strength**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**neurological exam helps to differentiate from entrapment syndromes**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "the following maneuvers exacerbate pain at lateral epicondyle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "resisted wrist extension with elbow fully extended and forearm pronated",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "resisted extension of the long fingers",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "maximal flexion of the wrist",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "passive wrist flexion in pronation causes pain at the elbow",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "resisted extension of the 3rd digit of the hand leads to pain over the lateral epicondyle (Maudsley's test)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "rule out intraarticular pathology and elbow instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "LUCL insufficiency",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "chair test",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "push up test",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "intraarticular pathology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "OCD and arthritis: decreased ROM",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "posterolateral plica: pain/clicking with passive elbow flexion in pronation and supination",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP/Lateral of elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually normal and very rarely change management",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may reveal calcifications near the lateral epicondyle (up to half of patients)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may reveal signs of previous surgery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "not necessary for diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may be helpful to rule out other potential sources of pain if diagnosis is unclear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**increased signal intensity at ECRB tendon** origin may be seen (up to 90% of cases)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/mri%20elbow.jpg",
                  "caption": "T2 coronal MRI with lateral epicondylitis"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/screen_shot_2016-06-21_at_2.24.30_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": "T2 coronal MRI"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3082/images/screen_shot_2016-06-21_at_2.24.23_pm_(2).jpg",
                  "caption": "Axial T2"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "thickening or thinning",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "edema",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tendon degeneration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings are not associated with symptom severity and should not dictate management",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasonography",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "requires experienced operator (variable sensitivity/specificity)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most useful diagnostic tool in experienced operator hands",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ECRB tendon appears thickened and hypoechoic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "histopathological studies of the ECRB tendon tissue shows",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**fibroblast hypertrophy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**disorganized collagen**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**vascular hyperplasia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "No inflammatory changes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diagnosis is primarily based on symptoms and physical exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Posterolateral plica",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Posterolateral rotatory instability",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Radial tunnel syndrome**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "palpation 3-4 cm distal and anterior to the lateral epicondyle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain with resisted third-finger extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain with resisted forearm supination",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Occult fracture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Cervical radiculopathy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Capitellar osteochondritis dissecans",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Triceps tendinitis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Radiocapitellar osteoarthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Osteochondritis dissecans",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Shingles",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity modification, ice, NSAIDS, physical therapy, ultrasound",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "NSAIDs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "may have short-term benefit, but increased risk of GI side effects",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tennis modifications (slower playing surface, more flexible racquet, lower string tension, larger grip)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "counter-force brace (strap)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**steroid injections**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "controversial after an RCT compared steroids versus placebo and found equivalent pain, grip strength, and patient-reported outcomes.",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "may have detrimental effects on muscle and skin",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "physical therapy regimen",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "acupuncture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "iontophoresis/phonophoresis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Platelet-rich plasma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "more efficacious for long-term pain relief, tendon healing, and improved function when compared to steroid injections",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "extracorporeal shock wave therapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "no difference shown at 6 months compared to placebo",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Nitroglycerin patch",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "80-90% improve with nonoperative treatment at 1 year",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "only 2-4% eventually undergo surgical intervention",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no nonoperative protocol has proven superior to observation or placebo",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "release and debridement of ECRB origin",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if prolonged nonoperative (12 months) fails",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "clear diagnosis (isolated lateral epicondylitis)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "intra-articular pathology",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may be performed open or arthroscopic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "contraindications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "inadequate trial of nonsurgical treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patient noncompliance with the recommended nonsurgical treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "no difference in outcomes between open and arthroscopic procedures (patient satisfaction, return to work, and complications)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "90-100% of patients have improvements in symptoms, but up to 40% have persistent pain",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Release and debridement of ECRB origin**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "incision is positioned over the common extensor origin",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lift ECRL off of ECRB (located deep and posterior to ECRL)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Nirschl scratch test to assess for degenerative tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "excise degenerative tissue",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decorticate epicondyle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "watertight repair of capsule if breached to prevent synovial fistula",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "side-to-side closure of tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "reattach tendon to epicondyle using an anchor or bone tunnel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "arthroscopic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "advantages include visualization and ability to address intraarticular pathology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "resect lateral capsule anteriorly (do not pass midradial head to protect LUCL)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "release ECRB from its origin (where muscle tissue begins)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decorticate lateral epicondyle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Up to 40% of patients who undergo surgery still have some level of persistent pain",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Iatrogenic LUCL injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "excessive resection of the LUCL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "should not extend beyond equator of radial head",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may lead to posterolateral rotatory instability (PLRI)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Missed radial nerve entrapment syndrome**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common in up to 15% of patients with lateral epicondylitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Iatrogenic neurovascular injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "radial nerve injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Heterotopic ossification**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "decrease risk with thorough irrigation following decortication",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Stiffness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "especially if combined with an intraarticular procedure",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Infection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Missed concomitant pathology (i.e. PLRI, radial tunnel)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Non-operative treatment effective in up to 95% of cases",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Factors associated with increased likelihood of requiring operative management",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "depression, anxiety, and poor coping skills are greatest risk factors for poor outcome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ipsilateral radial tunnel syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "history of prior injection (any kind)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "workers' compensation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
